#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:74
msgid "Keep archived meetings of child involvements that are no longer shown"
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:76
msgid "When a child involvement's \"Show in Sites\" is turned off in TouchPoint, its meetings are normally removed from your site.  Check this to keep its archived meetings (those older than \"Archive After Days\"), so past Editions stay complete.  Its upcoming meetings are still removed."
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:79
msgid "How each option works"
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:80
msgid "Options can be combined.  Any level that would contain only one item is skipped, so an Edition with only one meeting is just that meeting's page."
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:85
msgid "Meetings of child and grandchild involvements (that have \"Show in Sites\" checked) are shown within this involvement, instead of within their own involvements.  The child involvements are not listed separately, but the Register and RSVP buttons on their meetings still use the child involvement.  This is useful when parts of an event have their own registration or RSVP."
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:86
msgid "If this is not checked, child involvements are listed on their own, as usual."
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:93
msgid "Each occurrence of an event that happens again and again in the same involvement becomes an Edition, such as this year's conference and last year's.  A new Edition starts whenever there are more than 25 days between the end of one meeting and the start of the next.  Past Editions stay on your site with their original descriptions."
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:100
msgid "Meetings of the same involvement are grouped into a Cluster:"
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:102
msgid "Back-to-back meetings form a Cluster: no more than 2 hours apart, with no other meeting between them.  For example, a memorial service and its reception.  Meetings on different days are never grouped this way."
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:103
msgid "Within an Edition, all of a child involvement's meetings form one Cluster, even if they're on different days.  For example, two performances of the same concert."
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:109
msgid "Previous behavior"
msgstr ""

#: src/templates/admin/mtgGroupingKoForm.php:111
msgid "Meetings of the same involvement that start less than 23 hours apart are collected together, as in earlier versions of TouchPoint-WP.  Each post type keeps the \"Collect Meetings for Larger Events\" setting it had before.  This option is available because your site used it before upgrading, so that nothing changes until you choose."
msgstr ""

